---
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Should I Spend $30,000 on a Wedding?</title>
    <meta
  name="description"
  content="Use this wedding affordability calculator to determine whether a $30,000 wedding fits your income, savings, debt load, and long-term financial goals."
/>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #eef2f7;
        --card: #ffffff;
        --navy: #0f172a;
        --text: #111827;
        --muted: #475569;
        --teal: #0f766e;
        --green: #15803d;
        --amber: #b45309;
        --red: #b91c1c;
        --border: #d7dee8;
      }

      body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        background: var(--bg);
        margin: 0;
        padding: 40px 20px;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      .container {
        max-width: 920px;
        margin: auto;
      }
.content-section {
  max-width: 760px;
  margin: 0 auto 48px auto;
}

.content-section h2 {
  font-size: 2rem;
  margin-bottom: 24px;
  line-height: 1.2;
}

.content-section p {
  font-size: 1.08rem;
  line-height: 1.9;
  color: #334155;
  margin-bottom: 24px;
}
      .eyebrow {
        text-align: center;
        color: var(--teal);
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: .08em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        margin-bottom: 14px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 56px;
        text-align: center;
        margin: 0 0 16px;
        color: var(--navy);
        line-height: 1.05;
      }

      .subtitle {
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 22px;
        color: var(--muted);
        margin: 0 auto 42px;
        line-height: 1.5;
        max-width: 760px;
      }

      .calculator {
        background: var(--card);
        border-radius: 24px;
        padding: 38px;
        box-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
        border: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
      }

      .calculator h2 {
        margin-top: 0;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      .grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 20px;
      }

      label {
        display: block;
        font-weight: 800;
        margin-bottom: 9px;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      input {
        width: 100%;
        padding: 16px;
        border-radius: 12px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        font-size: 18px;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      input:focus {
        outline: 3px solid rgba(15, 118, 110, 0.18);
        border-color: var(--teal);
      }

      button {
        margin-top: 28px;
        background: var(--navy);
        color: white;
        border: none;
        padding: 18px 28px;
        border-radius: 14px;
        font-size: 19px;
        font-weight: 900;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      button:hover {
        background: var(--teal);
      }

      .result {
        margin-top: 34px;
        background: #f8fafc;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 20px;
        padding: 30px;
        display: none;
      }

      .score {
        font-size: 36px;
        font-weight: 900;
        margin-bottom: 18px;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      .bar {
        height: 16px;
        background: #e2e8f0;
        border-radius: 999px;
        overflow: hidden;
        margin-bottom: 24px;
      }

      .bar-fill {
        height: 100%;
        background: var(--teal);
        width: 0%;
      }

      .line {
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        font-size: 18px;
        color: var(--text);
      }

      .guidance {
        margin-top: 26px;
        font-size: 20px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--navy);
      }

      .verdict-breakdown {
  margin-top: 18px;
  padding: 18px;
  background: #f8fafc;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 14px;
  font-size: 0.98rem;
  line-height: 1.65;
  color: var(--muted);
  display: none;
}

.verdict-breakdown strong {
  color: var(--text);
}

      .disclaimer {
        margin-top: 22px;
        font-size: 13px;
        color: #64748b;
      }

      @media (max-width: 700px) {
        body {
          padding: 28px 14px;
        }

        h1 {
          font-size: 38px;
        }

        .subtitle {
          font-size: 18px;
        }

        .calculator {
          padding: 24px;
        }

        .grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
      }
      .card {
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 20px;
  padding: 24px;
}

.card h3 {
  font-size: 1.35rem;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  line-height: 1.3;
}

.card p {
  color: #475569;
  line-height: 1.7;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.card-category {
  color: var(--teal);
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">Wedding Spending Calculator</div>

      <h1>Should I Spend $30,000 on a Wedding?</h1>

      <p class="subtitle">
        Get a practical verdict based on income, savings, debt, stress level,
        and how much of your financial cushion the wedding would consume.
      </p>
<section class="content-section">
  <h2>How Much Wedding Can You Actually Afford?</h2>

  <p>
    Weddings are one of the largest discretionary expenses most people will
    ever make. While the average American wedding now costs tens of thousands
    of dollars, affordability depends far more on income, savings, debt load,
    and long-term financial flexibility than on social expectations.
  </p>

  <p>
    A $30,000 wedding may feel manageable for one household and financially
    dangerous for another. The real question is not whether the wedding is
    "worth it," but whether the expense damages emergency savings, increases
    debt stress, or delays larger financial goals like homeownership,
    retirement investing, or starting a family.
  </p>

  <p>
    This calculator helps estimate whether a wedding budget fits comfortably
    within your broader financial picture by analyzing savings impact, debt
    ratio, and income flexibility.
  </p>
</section>
      <div class="calculator">
        <h2>Wedding Affordability Verdict</h2>

        <div class="grid">
          <div>
            <label>Combined Annual Income</label>
            <input id="income" type="number" placeholder="Example: 140000" />
          </div>

          <div>
            <label>Total Savings</label>
            <input id="savings" type="number" placeholder="Example: 50000" />
          </div>

          <div>
            <label>Wedding Cost</label>
            <input id="cost" type="number" placeholder="30000" />
          </div>

          <div>
            <label>Current Debt</label>
            <input id="debt" type="number" placeholder="Example: 12000" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <button id="weddingButton">Get Wedding Verdict</button>

        <div class="result" id="result">
          <div class="score" id="scoreText"></div>

          <div class="bar">
            <div class="bar-fill" id="barFill"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="line" id="stress"></div>
          <div class="line" id="savingsImpact"></div>
          <div class="line" id="incomeImpact"></div>
          <div class="line" id="debtRatio"></div>

          <div class="guidance" id="guidance"></div>

          <div class="verdict-breakdown" id="verdictBreakdown"></div>

          <div class="disclaimer">
            This is a general educational estimate, not financial advice.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <section class="content-section">
  <h2>What Your Wedding Verdict Actually Means</h2>

  <p>
    A wedding affordability score is not a judgment about whether a celebration
    is emotionally meaningful or personally worthwhile. The purpose of the
    verdict is to estimate how much financial pressure the expense may create
    relative to your current income, savings cushion, and debt load.
  </p>

  <p>
    Higher savings impact percentages usually indicate that the wedding budget
    may consume too much of an emergency fund or reduce future financial
    flexibility. Large wedding expenses become more financially dangerous when
    they rely heavily on financing, credit cards, personal loans, or depleted
    savings accounts.
  </p>

  <p>
    Debt ratios also matter. Even higher-income households can create long-term
    financial stress if wedding spending significantly increases existing debt
    obligations or delays major goals like buying a home, investing for
    retirement, or building long-term savings stability.
  </p>

  <p>
    In general, the healthiest wedding budgets are the ones that allow couples
    to celebrate meaningfully without creating years of financial recovery
    afterward.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="content-section faq-section">
  <h2>Wedding Spending FAQ</h2>

  <h3>Is $30,000 too much to spend on a wedding?</h3>
  <p>
    It depends on income, savings, debt, and whether the wedding creates
    financial stress afterward. A $30,000 wedding may be manageable for one
    household and risky for another.
  </p>

  <h3>Should you finance a wedding?</h3>
  <p>
    Financing a wedding can create long-term pressure after the celebration is
    over. If the cost requires credit cards, personal loans, or depleted
    emergency savings, the budget may be too aggressive.
  </p>

  <h3>How much of your savings should a wedding use?</h3>
  <p>
    There is no perfect number, but using a large share of available savings can
    reduce financial flexibility. Emergency savings, housing goals, debt, and
    future plans should come before a larger wedding budget.
  </p>

  <h3>What percentage of income should a wedding cost?</h3>
  <p>
    A lower percentage of annual income is usually safer. The higher the wedding
    cost rises relative to income, the more important it becomes to avoid debt
    and preserve savings.
  </p>
</section>
<section class="content-section">
  <h2>Related Financial Calculators</h2>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-category">Travel</div>
      <h3>Should I Spend $5,000 on a Vacation?</h3>
      <p>
        Evaluate whether a large vacation expense fits your income, savings,
        debt load, and long-term flexibility.
      </p>

      <a class="button" href="/should-i-spend-5000-on-a-vacation">
        Open Calculator
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-category">Cars</div>
      <h3>Should I Spend $700 on a Car Payment?</h3>
      <p>
        Analyze whether your monthly vehicle payment is realistic based on
        income, debt, and financial cushion.
      </p>

      <a class="button" href="/should-i-spend-700-on-a-car-payment">
        Open Calculator
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
    </div>

    <script is:inline>
      function calculateWedding() {
        const income = Number(document.getElementById("income").value);
        const savings = Number(document.getElementById("savings").value);
        const cost = Number(document.getElementById("cost").value);
        const debt = Number(document.getElementById("debt").value || 0);

        if (!income || !savings || !cost) {
          alert("Please enter income, savings, and wedding cost.");
          return;
        }

        const savingsImpact = (cost / savings) * 100;
        const incomeImpact = (cost / income) * 100;
        const debtRatio = (debt / income) * 100;
        const breakdown = document.getElementById("verdictBreakdown");

        let score = 100;

        if (savingsImpact > 10) score -= 12;
        if (savingsImpact > 25) score -= 18;
        if (savingsImpact > 50) score -= 25;
        if (incomeImpact > 15) score -= 10;
        if (incomeImpact > 25) score -= 15;
        if (debtRatio > 10) score -= 8;
        if (debtRatio > 25) score -= 12;

        score = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, score));

        let verdict = "";
        let guidance = "";
        let stress = "";
        let barColor = "";

        if (score >= 85) {
          verdict = "Smart Wedding Budget";
          stress = "Low stress";
          barColor = "var(--green)";
          guidance = "This wedding appears financially manageable. It still deserves a budget, but the cost does not seriously threaten your cushion.";
        } else if (score >= 70) {
          verdict = "Manageable with Guardrails";
          stress = "Manageable stress";
          barColor = "var(--teal)";
          guidance = "This can work if you avoid financing it, keep extra costs under control, and preserve enough savings after the wedding.";
        } else if (score >= 50) {
          verdict = "Proceed Carefully";
          stress = "Noticeable stress";
          barColor = "var(--amber)";
          guidance = "This wedding would take a meaningful bite out of your financial cushion. Consider trimming the guest list, venue cost, or extras.";
        } else {
          verdict = "High Financial Risk";
          stress = "High stress";
          barColor = "var(--red)";
          guidance = "This wedding cost looks too aggressive for the current financial picture. A smaller budget would likely protect your future flexibility.";
        }

        document.getElementById("result").style.display = "block";
        document.getElementById("scoreText").textContent = `${verdict} - ${score}/100`;
        document.getElementById("barFill").style.width = `${score}%`;
        document.getElementById("barFill").style.background = barColor;

        document.getElementById("stress").innerHTML =
          `<strong>Stress level:</strong> ${stress}`;

        document.getElementById("savingsImpact").innerHTML =
          `<strong>Savings impact:</strong> ${savingsImpact.toFixed(1)}% of savings`;

        document.getElementById("incomeImpact").innerHTML =
          `<strong>Income impact:</strong> ${incomeImpact.toFixed(1)}% of annual income`;

        document.getElementById("debtRatio").innerHTML =
          `<strong>Debt ratio:</strong> ${debtRatio.toFixed(1)}% of annual income`;

        document.getElementById("guidance").textContent = guidance;

breakdown.style.display = "block";

breakdown.innerHTML = `
  <strong>Financial Breakdown:</strong><br><br>

  - Wedding cost equals <strong>${incomeImpact.toFixed(1)}%</strong> of annual household income.<br>

  - Wedding cost consumes <strong>${savingsImpact.toFixed(1)}%</strong> of total savings.<br>

  - Existing debt load equals <strong>${debtRatio.toFixed(1)}%</strong> of annual income.<br><br>

  Higher savings impact and debt pressure usually increase long-term financial stress after large purchases.
`;
      }

      document.getElementById("weddingButton").addEventListener("click", calculateWedding);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>